      "content": "wait, so you're saying that teaching kids about systemic injustice might actually be \"divisive\" or make them \"defensive\"? that feels like a pretty heavy way to frame it. if we prioritize \"pride and belonging\" over teaching the truth about how power works, aren't we just choosing to leave them unprepared for the real world? it seems like your recommendation is basically saying we should delay the hard truths until they aren't \"painful\" anymore. isn't that just avoiding the actual issues?",
